                                                "text": "‘Well, I’ll bet you half a dozen of claret on it; come!’ said Wilkins Flasher, Esquire, resuming the conversation to which Mr. Pell’s entrance had caused a momentary interruption.\n[…] ‘I never bet half a dozen!’ said the other gentleman. ‘I’ll take a dozen.’\n‘Done, Simmery, done!’ said Wilkins Flasher, Esquire.\n‘P. P., mind,’ observed the other."
